# Minimalist Flask Library Project 📚

A clean, elegant web application built with **Flask** and **SQLite** to manage your personal book collection. This project features full CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) functionality wrapped in a custom, high-end minimalist aesthetic with warm beige-brown tones.

---

## ✨ Features

- **Full CRUD Operations:** 
  - **Create:** Add new books with titles, authors, and ratings.
  - **Read:** View your entire library collection on a clean home page list.
  - **Update:** Edit existing book ratings with robust input validation (0–10 range checks).
  - **Delete:** Remove books from your collection instantly.
- **Custom Minimalist UI:** Designed with an editorial aesthetic featuring a warm cream background, serif headings (`Georgia`), soft cocoa-brown text, and smooth hover states.
- **Enhanced UX:** Features global hyperlink styling and automatic form field autofocus so you can start typing right away.
- **Persistent Storage:** Powered by SQLite and Flask-SQLAlchemy for seamless data management.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- **Backend:** Python, Flask, Flask-SQLAlchemy
- **Database:** SQLite (`books-collection.db`)
- **Frontend:** HTML5, CSS3 (Custom centralized stylesheet)

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```text
library-project/
│
├── main.py                 # Main Flask application and routes
├── instance/
│   └── books-collection.db # SQLite database
├── static/
│   └── style.css           # Centralized minimalist stylesheet
└── templates/
    ├── index.html          # Home page (Book list view)
    ├── add.html            # Add book form
    └── edit.html           # Edit rating form
